@extends('layouts/buddy')
@section('title', 'Buddy Rover adventure carrier')
@section('description', 'Meet Buddy Rover. An adventure carrier designed around long-distance running, beach walks and winter routes, with big dogs in mind.')
@section('social_image', 'https://buddywheels.org/images/buddy-rover.webp')
@section('head')
  <link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ initialImage }}">
@endsection
<script server>
import { splitFinish as splitServerFinish, defaultFinish as serverDefaultFinish } from '~/app/Storefront/Finish'
export let initialFinish = serverDefaultFinish
try { initialFinish = splitServerFinish(requestContext.query()).finish } catch {}
const finishForm = 'rover-purchase'
import { roverConfigurations, money } from '~/app/Storefront/Catalog'
export const configurations = roverConfigurations.map(item => ({ ...item, priceLabel: money(item.price), image: item.code === 'snow' ? '/images/buddy-rover-snow.webp' : '/images/buddy-rover.webp', imageAlt: item.code === 'snow' ? 'Buddy Rover ski conversion with twin skis and tow harness on a groomed winter route' : 'Buddy Rover running carrier with a golden retriever on a firm beach path', shown: item.code === 'snow' ? 'Snow configuration shown.' : 'Run configuration shown.' }))
const requested = requestContext.query().mode
export const initialMode = configurations.some(item => item.code === requested) ? requested : 'run'
const first = configurations.find(item => item.code === initialMode)!
const initialSlug = first.slug
const initialImage = first.image
const initialAlt = first.imageAlt
defineClientPayload({ initialFinish, configurations, initialMode })
</script>
<script client>
import { finishQuery } from '~/app/Storefront/Finish'
const accent = state(initialFinish.accent)
const trim = state(initialFinish.trim)
const finish = derived(() => ({ accent: accent(), trim: trim() }))
const mode = state(initialMode)
const selected = derived(() => configurations.find(item => item.code === mode()) || configurations[0]!)
</script>
@section('content')
  <div class="py-6 shell"><ProductFamilyNav active="rover" /></div>
  <section class="pb-16 product-layout shell">
    <div class="product-media"><figure class="product-photo rover-photo"><img src="{{ initialImage }}" :src="selected().image" :srcset="selected().image.replace('.webp', '-640.webp') + ' 640w, ' + selected().image + ' 1280w'" sizes="(max-width:1023px) calc(100vw - 40px), 55vw" alt="{{ initialAlt }}" :alt="selected().imageAlt" width="1280" height="853" fetchpriority="high"></figure><p class="mt-3 text-xs muted">{{ selected().shown }}</p>
      <div class="grid gap-5 grid-cols-2 mt-7"><div class="feature-rule"><h2 class="font-semibold text-base">Your pace. Their place.</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">Designed around long-distance running, with a roomy cabin for the companion who comes along for the miles.</p></div><div class="feature-rule"><h2 class="font-semibold text-base">Walk in, no step.</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">The tailgate folds down into a gentle ramp, for the dog who can no longer jump or step up.</p></div></div>
      <div class="grid gap-5 grid-cols-2"><div class="feature-rule"><h2 class="font-semibold text-base">Ready for the weather.</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">A pitched roof for rain, roll-down clear panels for wind and shaded mesh for sun. Weather testing comes before any claim.</p></div><div class="feature-rule"><h2 class="font-semibold text-base">A repairable adventure starts here.</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">A metal chassis with replaceable fabric, running gear and printable service parts.</p></div></div><div class="feature-rule"><h2 class="font-semibold text-base">See how it is built.</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">Turn the frame, lower the ramp and download the bench design, parts list and printable files.</p><a href="/design-studio-rover" :href="'/design-studio-rover?' + finishQuery(finish())" class="inline-flex mt-3 button-text" data-rover-studio-link>Open the Rover 3D studio</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="product-info"><p class="eyebrow">A seat for your best friend.</p><h1 class="mt-3 section-title">Buddy Rover</h1><p class="mt-4 muted">For the long run, the slow beach walk, and the dog who belongs beside you.</p><div class="flex gap-4 items-center mt-6"><p class="price" data-rover-price>{{ selected().priceLabel }}</p><span class="text-xs muted">USD</span></div>
      <fieldset class="mt-7 p-0 border-0"><legend class="mb-3 font-semibold text-sm">Choose your adventure</legend><div class="grid gap-2 grid-cols-2">
        <button type="button" class="mode-button" data-mode="run" :aria-pressed="mode() === 'run' ? 'true' : 'false'" @click="mode.set('run')"><strong>Run</strong><span>Long miles &amp; daily paths</span></button>
        <button type="button" class="mode-button" data-mode="coast" :aria-pressed="mode() === 'coast' ? 'true' : 'false'" @click="mode.set('coast')"><strong>Coast</strong><span>Beach walks &amp; shorelines</span></button>
        <button type="button" class="mode-button" data-mode="snow" :aria-pressed="mode() === 'snow' ? 'true' : 'false'" @click="mode.set('snow')"><strong>Snow</strong><span>Winter routes &amp; ski days</span></button>
        <button type="button" class="mode-button" data-mode="all-season" :aria-pressed="mode() === 'all-season' ? 'true' : 'false'" @click="mode.set('all-season')"><strong>All-season</strong><span>The complete collection</span></button>
      </div></fieldset>
      <div class="mt-4 configuration-note" aria-live="polite"><h2 class="font-semibold text-base" data-rover-name>{{ selected().name }}</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">{{ selected().description }}</p></div>
      @include('../partials/finish-controls')
      <form id="rover-purchase" action="/api/cart/add" method="POST" class="mt-6"><input type="hidden" name="slug" value="{{ initialSlug }}" :value="selected().slug"><input type="hidden" name="redirect" value="/cart"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center"><QuantitySelector :value="1" :min="1" :max="5" label="Rover quantity" /><span class="hidden md:block"><Button type="submit" variant="bare" class="button-primary">Add to basket</Button></span></div></form>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs availability muted"><span class="availability-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Orders opening soon. Save your selection in the basket.</p>
      <div class="mt-7 faq"><details open><summary>In your configuration</summary><ul class="configuration-list"><li>{{ selected().included[0] }}</li><li>{{ selected().included[1] }}</li><li>{{ selected().included[2] }}</li></ul><p>Configuration contents are the design brief. Final specifications and use limits will be confirmed before orders open.</p></details><details><summary>A running setup with a purpose.</summary><p>The Run configuration centers on a three-wheel layout, a forward running wheel, a push handle, brake and wrist tether. Distance, speed and load limits will come from whole-system testing.</p></details><details><summary>What changes for the beach?</summary><p>Coast adds a wider-wheel conversion and easy-clean surfaces to the running configuration. Packed shoreline paths are the starting point. Deep loose sand, steep dunes and saltwater immersion are outside the initial use brief.</p></details><details><summary>And when the snow arrives?</summary><p>Snow pairs the cabin with a dedicated ski conversion and tow harness for groomed winter routes. The ski setup requires its own stability, attachment and stopping tests.</p></details><details><summary>How does my dog get in?</summary><p>The current design lowers the tailgate into a ramp of about nine degrees, with side curbs and a grip surface, so there is no step to climb. It is a bench design and has not been tested with a dog. <a href="/design-studio-rover" class="underline">See the ramp in 3D.</a></p></details><details><summary>Will my dog have enough room?</summary><p>Measure seated height, lying length and shoulder width, including space to change position. Cabin dimensions and load limits will be published after validation. <a href="/fit-guide#rover" class="underline">See the Rover measuring guide.</a></p></details></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section-space story-band"><div class="shell"><h2 class="section-title">Keep them part of the day.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl muted">Some dogs want the walk but need a ride for the rest. Others have always been your running partner. Rover starts with the same thought: there should still be a place for them.</p><a href="/care#rover" class="inline-flex mt-6 button-text">A few good habits for every outing</a></div></section>
  <div class="mobile-purchase"><div><span class="text-xs muted">{{ selected().label }} configuration</span><strong>{{ selected().priceLabel }}</strong></div><button id="rover-mobile-add" form="rover-purchase" type="submit" class="button-primary">Add to basket</button></div>
@endsection
